{'symbol': 'MMM', 'date': '2020-05-14 10:30:00', 'title': '3M Says Mask Sales To Contribute 3% To Q2 sales growth -GS Conf', 'text': '3M CO CFO SAYS EXPECT TO BE PRODUCING AT RUN RATE OF 2 BILLION RESPIRATORS PER YEAR BY 2020 END -GOLDMAN SACHS CONF CALL.3M CO CFO SAYS MASK SALES COULD CONTRIBUTE 3% TO TOTAL COMPANY GROWTH IN Q2 -GOLDMAN SACHS CONF CALL.3M CO CFO SAYS SEEING NOTICEABLE SALES DECLINES IN TRANSPORTATION AND ELECTRONICS UNITS IN JAPAN -GOLDMAN SACHS CONF CALL.3M CO CFO SAYS WATCHING UNDERLYING DEMAND IN CHINA AFTER 7% GROWTH IN APRIL -GOLDMAN SACHS CONF CALL.3M CO CFO SAYS SEEING STRENGTH IN AIR QUALITY SOLUTIONS.3M CO CFO SAYS ORAL CARE BUSINESS WAS DOWN 70% IN APRIL.3M CO CFO SAYS EXPECT AUTOMOTIVE BUSINESS TO BE DOWN DRAMATICALLY IN Q2.3M CO CFO SAYS STATIONARY AND OFFICE PRODUCTS ALSO SEEING BIG DECLINES IN Q2.3M CO CFO SAYS A RECOVERY WILL BE LINKED TO HOW SOON END MARKETS CAN SNAP BACK.3M CO CFO SAYS EXPECT MANY Q2 COST SAVING ACTIONS TO CONTINUE IN Q3 AND Q4.3M CO CFO SAYS SEEING SOME PFAS-RELATED COURT DATES BEING DELAYED.3M CO CFO SAYS SMART PHONE DEMAND IS STILL DOWN, SEEING GROWTH IN LAPTOPS.3M CO CFO SAYS OVERALL OPTIMISTIC ABOUT ELECTRONICS BUSINESS GIVEN 5G PROSPECTS.3M CO CFO SAYS DON’T ANTICIPATE ANY SIZABLE ACQUISITION IN THE NEAR TERM.3M CO CFO SAYS, FROM AN EBITDA PERSPECTIVE, ACELITY ACQUISITION IS EXCEEDING CO’S EXPECTATIONS.'}
